<title>TURKEY: TURK GARANTI BANK Q1 NET UP 275.2 PCT.</title>
<headline>TURK GARANTI BANK Q1 NET UP 275.2 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-March 1997 provisional</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira)    648.27 vs     388.76</p>
<p>    Net profit		  11,668.86 vs   3,110.08</p>
<p>    Net interest income     22,192.17 vs   8,545.95</p>
<p>    Net non-interest expense 6,702.45 vs   5,233.66</p>
<p>    Provisions for bad loans     1.82 vs	 0</p>
<p>    Loans			276,134.34 vs  96,198.95</p>
<p>    Deposits		   217,386.69 vs 100,454.50</p>
<p>    Loans borrowed	   172,882.41 vs  58,242.51</p>
<p>    Equity			38,140.03 vs 15,530.82</p>
<p>    Capital		     18,000.00 vs   8,000.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Turkiye Garanti Bankas A.S., a leading commercial bank, is largely owned by finance, construction, food and trade group Dogus.</p>
<p>The bank will raise its capital to 40 trillion lira by issuing 0.7864 right and 0.4358 bonus for one existing share from May 9.</p>
<p>Garanti sold its 85.54 percent stake in its banking subsidiary Bankekspres for $85 million to contractor Korkmaz Yigit at end-March. Profit from the sale will be used to finance the bonus issue.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 77 percent annual wholesale in March.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875. ATA EKS</p>
</text>
